1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,300
In Chapter 14 of Nekros,
the crime scene is…

2
00:00:02,943 --> 00:00:03,850
A warehouse by the pier.

3
00:00:04,777 --> 00:00:07,650
Are you saying Kaye is Mr. Kill, Praew?

4
00:00:08,838 --> 00:00:11,760
You’re the only person who knows
what’s going on in the murderer’s head.

5
00:00:11,911 --> 00:00:12,739
Work with me.

6
00:00:13,053 --> 00:00:16,022
The victim in Chapter 18 of Nekros
is a dirty politician.

7
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:19,050
The MP is recently
taking a meditation retreat

8
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:20,583
at a temple in the suburbs.

9
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:22,096
Can I ask you something?

10
00:00:22,746 --> 00:00:24,179
Why did you write Nekros?

11
00:00:24,510 --> 00:00:25,696
My family was ruined

12
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:29,453
because of the Thai Investment Bank case.

13
00:00:32,177 --> 00:00:35,340
I’ll prove to you

14
00:00:36,650 --> 00:00:37,460
that this world

15
00:00:39,030 --> 00:00:41,022
doesn’t need a monster like Nekros.

16
00:00:57,013 --> 00:00:58,259
Someone’s trying to break in.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:00:59,419
Get ready to seize him!

18
00:01:07,037 --> 00:01:07,697
Let go!
Who the hell are you?

19
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:10,543
I said let go of me!

20
00:01:11,728 --> 00:01:13,053
Why are you restraining me?

21
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:18,216
It’s not what you think, officer.

22
00:01:18,235 --> 00:01:19,096
I’m just…

23
00:01:29,174 --> 00:01:30,225
I’m a reporter.

24
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,534
Reporter?

25
00:01:33,922 --> 00:01:34,810
What are you doing here?

26
00:01:35,191 --> 00:01:35,980
I…

27
00:01:36,874 --> 00:01:39,800
(Sir, multiple cars
are approaching the temple’s gate.)

28
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:08,451
Try and take as much footage as possible.

29
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:14,059
You two, just take some photos
with the small cameras.

30
00:03:14,078 --> 00:03:14,980
No need to come in.
Yes.

31
00:03:15,805 --> 00:03:16,573
Let’s go.

32
00:03:17,183 --> 00:03:17,820
Come on.

33
00:03:31,053 --> 00:03:31,819
Stay calm.

34
00:03:32,145 --> 00:03:32,983
Stay calm.

35
00:03:33,285 --> 00:03:34,317
I’m a police officer.

36
00:03:34,333 --> 00:03:34,860
Please stay calm.

37
00:03:34,878 --> 00:03:36,856
MP Jaratphong is here, isn’t he?

38
00:03:36,896 --> 00:03:38,013
We just need an interview.

39
00:03:38,030 --> 00:03:39,220
No, you can’t. Please stay calm.

40
00:03:39,334 --> 00:03:40,380
Excuse me.

41
00:03:40,819 --> 00:03:43,220
Mr. MP is unavailable
for an interview right now.

42
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:44,354
Thank you.

43
00:03:45,574 --> 00:03:46,456
Unavailable?

44
00:03:46,478 --> 00:03:47,619
It will only take a minute!

45
00:03:50,534 --> 00:03:52,090
So the video with those women is real?

46
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:55,002
Phat?

47
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:58,995
What do you think
you’re doing to my friend?

48
00:04:00,271 --> 00:04:02,090
Oh, no. This is my brother.

49
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,600
It’s nothing.

50
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:08,398
Phat.

51
00:04:08,619 --> 00:04:10,820
Are you here because of
that leaked video, too?

52
00:04:11,940 --> 00:04:12,798
What video?

53
00:04:13,256 --> 00:04:14,700
What are reporters doing here?

54
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:18,170
We’re here to ask the MP
about the leaked video.

55
00:04:18,339 --> 00:04:19,497
The temple sex tape.

56
00:04:20,100 --> 00:04:21,100
You don’t know that?

57
00:04:21,835 --> 00:04:22,774
Video? What video?

58
00:04:22,868 --> 00:04:24,500
Why don’t I show you?

59
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:27,302
It’s been trending.

60
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:31,610
TWO-FACED MP HAVING AN ORGY IN A TEMPLE.
RELIGIOUS MAN, MY FOOT.

61
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:37,900
If you’re not here because of this,
what are you here for?

62
00:04:42,230 --> 00:04:44,386
-Please stay calm.
-Is that sex tape real?

63
00:04:44,416 --> 00:04:45,976
Please stay calm.

64
00:04:46,162 --> 00:04:47,850
Why is the police getting involved?

65
00:04:48,404 --> 00:04:50,902
Don’t tell me the MP is hiring cops
as his private guards.

66
00:04:51,057 --> 00:04:51,910
That’s not the case.

67
00:04:51,934 --> 00:04:53,210
I’m just here to do my job.

68
00:04:53,401 --> 00:04:54,705
What sort of things are you here to do?

69
00:04:54,731 --> 00:04:55,903
Can you tell us that?

70
00:04:56,830 --> 00:04:57,736
Tell us.

71
00:04:57,755 --> 00:04:59,099
Just tell us.

72
00:04:59,337 --> 00:05:00,897
I’m the leader of this team.

73
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,600
I apologize but we cannot give you
any details right now.

74
00:05:06,257 --> 00:05:08,499
Police Major Yotsaphat Traikanawut.

75
00:05:09,783 --> 00:05:12,998
I believe I smell something fishy.

76
00:05:16,139 --> 00:05:18,398
Mr. Thun Thawikorn Putthanan.

77
00:05:19,108 --> 00:05:19,897
Isn’t it?

78
00:05:21,256 --> 00:05:22,700
You’re an amazing reporter.

79
00:05:23,577 --> 00:05:25,690
You’re quite famous, too.

80
00:05:27,543 --> 00:05:28,770
You must know a thing or two

81
00:05:29,216 --> 00:05:32,742
about press ethics
and the right of privacy.

82
00:05:34,536 --> 00:05:39,200
I think you’re investigating
the serial murder case

83
00:05:39,761 --> 00:05:42,001
concerning the manga Nekros.

84
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:46,499
It’s plain as day that the murderer
is still out there.

85
00:05:47,783 --> 00:05:52,700
I don’t think you have enough time
on your hand

86
00:05:53,030 --> 00:05:56,491
to be serving a random politician,

87
00:05:57,819 --> 00:06:03,703
not unless you think MP Jaratphong
could be Nekros’ next victim.

88
00:06:10,790 --> 00:06:12,339
Is that the case?

89
00:06:17,663 --> 00:06:19,094
It’s a goddamn small room!

90
00:06:19,117 --> 00:06:20,302
Keep freaking looking!

91
00:06:21,531 --> 00:06:22,303
Huh?

92
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:23,653
Did you find it?

93
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:26,410
Or are you waiting for me
to get thrown in jail first?

94
00:06:28,361 --> 00:06:30,259
Damn it, it’s a tiny room!

95
00:06:30,282 --> 00:06:31,496
We found the cameras, sir.

96
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:36,451
Shit!

97
00:06:37,463 --> 00:06:38,699
There must be a mole.

98
00:06:39,339 --> 00:06:40,570
Find him!

99
00:06:40,791 --> 00:06:43,798
And when I find out who did this,

100
00:06:44,576 --> 00:06:46,490
I’ll make sure his family
goes through hell!

101
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:49,690
Get it done as soon as possible.

102
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:51,696
You should leave, sir.

103
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,210
I’ll handle the rest.

104
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:55,200
Damn it!

105
00:06:55,470 --> 00:06:56,300
Sir!

106
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:57,777
Where are you going? What about us?

107
00:06:57,810 --> 00:06:59,702
Inspector, is that true?

108
00:06:59,820 --> 00:07:02,300
Is MP Jaratphong the next victim?

109
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:05,899
-Is that true?
-Is it true?

110
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:07,500
Well, Inspector?

111
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:12,502
Why not take this opportunity
to give us an update on the investigation?

112
00:07:13,059 --> 00:07:14,896
We’re all here, after all.

113
00:07:14,970 --> 00:07:16,598
He’s right, sir. You should.

114
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,296
The investigation is confidential right now.

115
00:07:20,684 --> 00:07:22,253
Once the time is right,

116
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:24,610
we’ll definitely hold a press conference.

117
00:07:26,451 --> 00:07:27,300
Alright.

118
00:07:27,915 --> 00:07:30,056
I’m just worried about the MP, is all.

119
00:07:30,522 --> 00:07:33,502
Seeing Nekros’ previous victims…

120
00:07:34,305 --> 00:07:37,497
It wouldn’t be a surprise
if the next victim was MP Jaratphong.

121
00:07:38,385 --> 00:07:41,002
Let’s hope that’s not the case.

122
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,170
MP Jaratphong is leaving!

123
00:07:50,337 --> 00:07:51,140
Look!
She’s right.

124
00:07:52,022 --> 00:07:52,854
Mr. MP!
Sir!

125
00:07:53,482 --> 00:07:54,202
Mr. MP!

126
00:07:54,890 --> 00:07:55,702
Mr. MP!

127
00:07:57,751 --> 00:07:58,610
We just need an interview.

128
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:07,142
Sir!

129
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:08,459
We just have a few questions.

130
00:08:08,739 --> 00:08:09,502
Sir! Sir!

131
00:08:10,223 --> 00:08:11,490
-Why are you doing this?
-Sir!

132
00:08:38,576 --> 00:08:39,779
We have a few questions!

133
00:08:42,979 --> 00:08:44,374
-Sir!
-Give us an interview!

134
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:49,459
Sir! Answer the questions!

135
00:09:26,891 --> 00:09:27,659
Wait!

136
00:09:28,130 --> 00:09:29,145
That’s not the MP!

137
00:09:29,617 --> 00:09:30,700
Who’s that?

138
00:09:31,017 --> 00:09:32,170
Where’s the real MP?

139
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:35,096
What the hell are those cops doing here?

140
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,345
And when this gets to my party,
I’m gonna be in trouble.

141
00:09:37,373 --> 00:09:38,930
I can’t be losing my MP chair.

142
00:09:45,902 --> 00:09:47,862
Why the hell did you stop?
Hurry up and take me to the car!

143
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:49,340
You want all those reporters to get here?

144
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:55,001
Wait, wait, wait!

145
00:10:35,198 --> 00:10:38,401
Are you sure it was MP Jaratphong?

146
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:45,099
It was quite dark, but…

147
00:10:46,130 --> 00:10:47,797
I’m sure it was him.

148
00:10:52,705 --> 00:10:54,050
Radio all police stations.

149
00:10:54,551 --> 00:10:55,697
Tell them this is urgent.

150
00:10:55,979 --> 00:10:58,577
Set up checkpoints scanning
every opaque white van

151
00:10:58,598 --> 00:11:01,096
within the 10-20 kilometer radius
from here.

152
00:11:01,605 --> 00:11:02,797
Every single van.

153
00:11:03,149 --> 00:11:04,100
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

154
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,500
Good work today, everyone.

155
00:11:09,937 --> 00:11:11,601
See you at the office tomorrow.

156
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:15,899
Inspector, the press is already writing
about MP Jaratphong.

157
00:11:20,742 --> 00:11:22,099
They work fast.

158
00:11:29,690 --> 00:11:30,600
Praew, go home.

159
00:11:31,028 --> 00:11:31,804
What?

160
00:11:32,414 --> 00:11:33,201
You’re hurting me.

161
00:11:33,690 --> 00:11:34,497
Let go.

162
00:11:37,537 --> 00:11:38,798
Did you sneak into my room

163
00:11:39,950 --> 00:11:42,253
to get information just
so Tun could have some headlines?

164
00:11:43,425 --> 00:11:44,700
Do you realize what he did?

165
00:11:46,976 --> 00:11:49,102
Reporters are making things harder.

166
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:53,400
That kind of news is
a window of opportunity for the murderer.

167
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:57,200
If that MP actually ended up dead,

168
00:11:57,910 --> 00:11:59,600
how would you reporters
take responsibility for this?

169
00:12:02,226 --> 00:12:03,597
You’re just an intern.

170
00:12:04,991 --> 00:12:06,410
You’re not even a real reporter.

171
00:12:09,014 --> 00:12:11,299
And stop letting that jerk
mess with your head!

172
00:12:11,737 --> 00:12:13,010
He’s just using you to get some scoop.

173
00:12:13,350 --> 00:12:15,296
No one’s messing with my head!

174
00:12:16,296 --> 00:12:17,804
I’m just being myself.

175
00:12:18,780 --> 00:12:21,103
And that MP is a bad guy.

176
00:12:23,030 --> 00:12:24,730
I might be an intern,

177
00:12:26,348 --> 00:12:28,801
but I’m just doing what I think is right.

178
00:12:29,499 --> 00:12:32,797
I don’t want to be ignorant like some cops

179
00:12:33,337 --> 00:12:35,302
or a dirty cop like Dad.

180
00:12:47,251 --> 00:12:51,204
Lies become truths

181
00:12:51,949 --> 00:12:54,463
if the person who knows the truth
chooses to stay silent.

182
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:57,899
I won’t let that happen.

183
00:13:00,174 --> 00:13:03,820
Thank you for choosing
to do the right thing.

184
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,496
Get in the car. I’ll give you a ride.

185
00:13:32,293 --> 00:13:33,099
It’s okay.

186
00:13:33,131 --> 00:13:34,500
I can go home by myself.

187
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:36,500
You should talk to your sister.

188
00:13:38,134 --> 00:13:38,897
Nah.

189
00:13:40,510 --> 00:13:41,598
I’ll give you a ride.

190
00:13:43,659 --> 00:13:46,002
Praew won’t listen to me anyway
whatever I say right now.

191
00:13:52,710 --> 00:13:53,537
Thank you.

192
00:14:13,648 --> 00:14:15,779
You can let me off here, Inspector.

193
00:14:16,256 --> 00:14:17,302
I know a shortcut.

194
00:14:17,337 --> 00:14:18,497
Sure.

195
00:14:18,979 --> 00:14:19,802
Thank you.

196
00:14:56,041 --> 00:14:56,997
Eat lots.

197
00:14:57,350 --> 00:14:59,000
And you gotta do something
other than sleeping.

198
00:15:04,216 --> 00:15:05,696
Why not just adopt them?

199
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:14,497
It’s better this way.

200
00:15:15,590 --> 00:15:17,099
If one day I’m gone,

201
00:15:18,130 --> 00:15:19,696
someone will take care of them.

202
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,502
Ever since I lost my family,

203
00:15:53,590 --> 00:15:54,897
I’ve been on my own.

204
00:15:56,752 --> 00:16:02,182
No one is ever there to knock some sense
into me when I do something wrong.

205
00:16:06,934 --> 00:16:08,096
That’s why I think

206
00:16:09,328 --> 00:16:14,699
even though your sister is being stubborn
or saying something mean to you,

207
00:16:16,090 --> 00:16:21,977
maybe she’s just trying to prove herself
to you as her brother.

208
00:16:28,905 --> 00:16:30,302
Don’t be mad at her.

209
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:33,010
And don’t blame yourself.

210
00:16:34,641 --> 00:16:37,096
I think, as a big brother,

211
00:16:38,540 --> 00:16:39,899
you’re already doing your best.

212
00:16:45,731 --> 00:16:49,401
You sure are talkative today.

213
00:16:50,989 --> 00:16:52,602
You usually aren’t.

214
00:16:55,457 --> 00:16:57,296
But… Thank you.

215
00:17:10,573 --> 00:17:11,299
Bye.

216
00:17:19,454 --> 00:17:22,001
Well, I’d better go.

217
00:17:22,982 --> 00:17:24,097
Goodnight, Inspector.

218
00:18:28,891 --> 00:18:32,200
(I don’t want to be ignorant
like some cops)

219
00:18:32,730 --> 00:18:34,699
or a dirty cop like Dad.

220
00:18:43,422 --> 00:18:44,200
Inspector.

221
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:48,142
This is the report of
the interrogation of everyone

222
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:49,782
on the night the MP disappeared.

223
00:18:56,500 --> 00:18:57,942
The head of security said

224
00:18:58,007 --> 00:19:01,090
one of the guards
took the MP out the back door.

225
00:19:01,423 --> 00:19:03,700
I asked him to show me who that guard was.

226
00:19:04,327 --> 00:19:07,797
But as it turned out, that man
faked his identity to secure this job.

227
00:19:08,325 --> 00:19:09,700
I’m already looking into that.

228
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:13,500
And the van?

229
00:19:14,094 --> 00:19:16,798
No report from any checkpoints
about any suspicious vans.

230
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:23,299
If that man really was Nekros,

231
00:19:24,230 --> 00:19:25,597
by the time we learned who he is,

232
00:19:26,130 --> 00:19:27,948
the MP would become a lifeless body.

233
00:19:39,650 --> 00:19:40,690
You have something to say?

234
00:19:41,619 --> 00:19:42,503
Go for it.

235
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:50,019
I’m not sure if this is useful,

236
00:19:50,034 --> 00:19:54,297
and I don’t know
if I remember everything correctly.

237
00:19:55,044 --> 00:19:56,370
What are you talking about?

238
00:19:58,420 --> 00:19:59,930
Can I have some paper?

239
00:20:29,801 --> 00:20:31,379
That’s an old model,

240
00:20:32,177 --> 00:20:33,702
but a popular one.

241
00:20:34,211 --> 00:20:35,182
It’s still too common.

242
00:20:39,423 --> 00:20:40,899
I remember something else.

243
00:21:15,962 --> 00:21:16,702
Here.

244
00:21:19,699 --> 00:21:21,502
I remember the dent in the car

245
00:21:21,637 --> 00:21:25,798
and the tattoo of the person
who likely took MP Jaratphong.

246
00:21:27,247 --> 00:21:29,217
That narrows it down.

247
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:33,954
Get our intel team to look into
any criminal records that went to court.

248
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:37,202
Even rumors or accusations.

249
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:40,300
Check all the places
with a history of crimes

250
00:21:40,601 --> 00:21:42,520
with the MP’s name involved.

251
00:21:43,053 --> 00:21:46,099
If you ever run into the man
who took the MP,

252
00:21:46,730 --> 00:21:50,497
by all means assume that
he is our killer, Nekros.

253
00:21:51,327 --> 00:21:52,299
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

254
00:21:57,213 --> 00:21:58,096
Thanks for this.

255
00:22:07,977 --> 00:22:09,500
I want you to try and remember…

256
00:22:10,487 --> 00:22:12,090
the last page of that manga.

257
00:22:15,550 --> 00:22:16,770
If you did,

258
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:19,297
it would be a big help to us.

259
00:22:23,437 --> 00:22:24,801
I believe in you.

260
00:22:29,226 --> 00:22:29,900
Of course.

261
00:22:37,065 --> 00:22:38,500
Can you show me that one?

262
00:22:38,552 --> 00:22:43,051
(From the video leaked on social media
regarding MP Jaratphong,)

263
00:22:43,352 --> 00:22:46,422
(which reporters were on location
to investigate two nights ago,)

264
00:22:46,565 --> 00:22:48,380
(including us at Thun Insight,)

265
00:22:48,407 --> 00:22:50,515
(it seems things have escalated.)

266
00:22:50,537 --> 00:22:51,582
That’s the guy.

267
00:22:51,614 --> 00:22:55,137
(MP Jaratphong disappeared
right in front of our eyes)

268
00:22:55,173 --> 00:22:57,970
(and Inspector
Yotsaphat Trikanawut’s team.)

269
00:22:58,400 --> 00:23:01,140
(Seeing as his team
is responsible for investigating…)

270
00:23:01,155 --> 00:23:03,900
(kidnappings and serial killers,)

271
00:23:04,140 --> 00:23:08,355
(it is quite notable that
there are three cases involving)

272
00:23:08,382 --> 00:23:09,490
(some form of corruption.)

273
00:23:10,110 --> 00:23:11,001
Thanks.

274
00:23:11,370 --> 00:23:14,570
(…a connection between these cases
and the manga, Nekros.)

275
00:23:21,943 --> 00:23:22,702
Hmm.

276
00:23:24,985 --> 00:23:25,746
Thanks.

277
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:30,497
(I don’t think it was a coincidence)

278
00:23:30,610 --> 00:23:34,259
(that the police officer responsible
for the case and his team)

279
00:23:34,285 --> 00:23:37,257
(was at the scene.)

280
00:23:37,287 --> 00:23:39,244
(I don’t think it is right
to assume, however.)

281
00:23:39,259 --> 00:23:44,402
(Whether MP Jaratphong is a good
or bad person, no one can confirm.)

282
00:23:44,819 --> 00:23:49,890
(as long as we do not have any proof,
the MP is an innocent man.)

283
00:23:50,256 --> 00:23:52,057
Can you find out
where this tattoo parlor is?

284
00:23:52,908 --> 00:23:54,502
It’s a mess online.

285
00:23:55,570 --> 00:23:57,582
I can’t tell what is true
and what is not anymore.

286
00:23:59,370 --> 00:24:01,195
Who’s to say it’s not all true,
Lieutenant?

287
00:24:02,139 --> 00:24:03,650
I know dude’s a jerk.

288
00:24:03,982 --> 00:24:05,902
I just didn’t expect him
to be down right evil.

289
00:24:07,379 --> 00:24:08,496
Any updates?

290
00:24:10,226 --> 00:24:11,300
There are two, sir.

291
00:24:14,702 --> 00:24:16,004
We found the van.

292
00:24:16,574 --> 00:24:19,204
After cross-referencing
from Kaye’s sketch,

293
00:24:19,785 --> 00:24:20,597
here it is.

294
00:24:20,982 --> 00:24:23,810
And one more thing,
from the sketch of the tattoo,

295
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:27,401
when cross-referencing
with criminal records and medical history,

296
00:24:27,881 --> 00:24:29,100
we got our guy.

297
00:24:31,320 --> 00:24:32,198
Thank you.

298
00:24:32,943 --> 00:24:34,001
His name is Kim.

299
00:24:34,500 --> 00:24:36,002
I’m looking for him.

300
00:24:38,730 --> 00:24:39,496
Good job.

301
00:24:40,210 --> 00:24:41,201
Excuse me, sir.

302
00:24:44,420 --> 00:24:45,499
Can I see that?

303
00:24:51,250 --> 00:24:52,299
You’re observant.

304
00:24:53,364 --> 00:24:54,899
And you’re very detail-oriented.

305
00:24:55,862 --> 00:24:57,897
No wonder you’re a popular manga artist.

306
00:25:00,268 --> 00:25:03,500
I’m not that observant
if I don’t remember everything.

307
00:25:04,220 --> 00:25:05,697
What I wrote, that is.

308
00:25:07,217 --> 00:25:08,100
It’s okay.

309
00:25:08,722 --> 00:25:11,502
If we put all our effort together
and actually catch Kim,

310
00:25:12,260 --> 00:25:13,739
we won’t need the manga anymore.

311
00:25:19,540 --> 00:25:20,300
Right.

312
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:31,930
PROTECTING BAD GUYS
WITH TAXPAYER MONEY IS INSANE.

313
00:25:31,960 --> 00:25:33,450
WHAT DO YOU EXPECT THE POLICE TO DO?
LET PEOPLE DIE?

314
00:25:33,520 --> 00:25:35,810
I BET THE POLICE WON’T LIFT A FINGER
IF THE VICTIMS AREN’T HIGH-PROFILE.

315
00:25:35,840 --> 00:25:38,130
HOW MANY BODIES DID HE CLAIM? IT’S SCARY.
I HOPE HE GETS CAUGHT SOON.

316
00:25:38,160 --> 00:25:41,170
ALL THE VICTIMS WERE CORRUPTING JERKS
WHO DESERVED IT.

317
00:25:41,200 --> 00:25:46,010
THERE’S TOO MUCH CORRUPTION
AND WE NEED SOMEONE TO REORGANIZE IT.

318
00:25:48,145 --> 00:25:50,002
Seems like the manga really won over.

319
00:25:52,200 --> 00:25:54,816
It’s just a trend, you know.

320
00:25:55,740 --> 00:25:59,398
I just… feel like
I’m doing something wrong

321
00:26:01,537 --> 00:26:04,200
when all I’ve been doing
is enforcing the law.

322
00:26:06,330 --> 00:26:07,802
It’s been three days now, too.

323
00:26:09,580 --> 00:26:11,296
And the situation hasn't improved.

324
00:26:13,760 --> 00:26:18,300
I bet I’m looking for a body
this time as well.

325
00:26:26,010 --> 00:26:29,299
Your sister is better at this
than you are, huh?

326
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:31,401
Look at Praew.

327
00:26:32,214 --> 00:26:34,500
No matter what mean things
you threw at her,

328
00:26:34,860 --> 00:26:36,090
she didn’t falter.

329
00:26:36,933 --> 00:26:39,598
She didn’t give up on her duty.

330
00:26:40,280 --> 00:26:42,802
So, you shouldn’t give up either.

331
00:26:44,500 --> 00:26:48,102
You know who you’re doing all this for.

332
00:26:58,840 --> 00:27:03,050
DO YOUR BEST, BRO.

333
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:06,440
PREAW SENT A STICKER.

334
00:27:08,220 --> 00:27:09,499
I’m lucky, aren’t I?

335
00:27:11,840 --> 00:27:13,219
I have a great sister.

336
00:27:16,380 --> 00:27:17,804
And I have a great partner.

337
00:27:46,903 --> 00:27:47,902
Inspector.

338
00:27:49,330 --> 00:27:50,699
We found where Kim’s laying low.

339
00:27:51,053 --> 00:27:52,460
We have eyes on it right now.

340
00:28:05,394 --> 00:28:06,202
Inspector.

341
00:28:06,914 --> 00:28:10,795
Our informant said Kim’s hideout
is on this street.

342
00:28:13,139 --> 00:28:14,850
This is the van.

343
00:28:15,447 --> 00:28:17,302
It’s the same van I saw the other night.

344
00:29:10,820 --> 00:29:11,600
Whoa…

345
00:29:12,939 --> 00:29:14,000
What a sicko.

346
00:29:33,765 --> 00:29:34,697
You okay?

347
00:29:38,900 --> 00:29:39,751
Yeah.

348
00:30:26,520 --> 00:30:29,090
MEMORIALS OF EVIL

349
00:30:45,780 --> 00:30:48,118
Does he have a notebook like this
for the other victims, too, I wonder…

350
00:30:51,899 --> 00:30:53,499
I don’t know anymore

351
00:30:54,580 --> 00:30:59,300
whether the victims or the murderer
that’s more of a sicko.

352
00:31:17,865 --> 00:31:19,200
Why don’t you wait outside?

353
00:31:20,711 --> 00:31:22,097
Let me handle it here.

354
00:31:46,397 --> 00:31:47,699
This is all the evidence we need.

355
00:31:48,400 --> 00:31:49,500
Issue an arrest warrant.

356
00:31:49,980 --> 00:31:50,937
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

357
00:31:55,680 --> 00:32:00,050
WANTED
ANAN PRATONNGAM, AGE: 26 FOR MURDER

358
00:32:29,160 --> 00:32:31,090
MEMORIALS OF EVIL

359
00:32:41,480 --> 00:32:42,247
Please…

360
00:32:42,282 --> 00:32:43,462
Please, let me go.

361
00:32:43,942 --> 00:32:45,502
Why are you doing this to me?

362
00:32:47,230 --> 00:32:49,080
I’ve never done anything to you.

363
00:32:49,485 --> 00:32:50,201
Please.

364
00:32:50,779 --> 00:32:51,597
Please.

365
00:32:52,099 --> 00:32:52,902
Please…

366
00:33:08,324 --> 00:33:09,502
Please.

367
00:33:09,857 --> 00:33:11,303
I’ve never done anything to you.

368
00:33:13,045 --> 00:33:14,219
No!

369
00:33:22,725 --> 00:33:24,201
It’s been three days.

370
00:33:25,448 --> 00:33:27,440
Are we to go back to
looking for a body again?

371
00:33:27,830 --> 00:33:30,000
It’s only been a few hours
since we released that wanted poster,

372
00:33:31,059 --> 00:33:33,290
and everyone online is already
lauding him as a hero.

373
00:33:34,060 --> 00:33:37,804
People are rooting for him
to kill MP Jaratphong before we catch him.

374
00:33:38,051 --> 00:33:39,600
What’s wrong with the world?

375
00:33:40,417 --> 00:33:41,903
How come we’re the bad guys here?

376
00:33:42,260 --> 00:33:44,200
Just focus on working
instead of complaining, Nop.

377
00:33:45,404 --> 00:33:47,001
Give me MP Jaratphong’s info.

378
00:33:47,542 --> 00:33:48,398
Yes, sir.

379
00:33:56,030 --> 00:33:56,899
Here it is.

380
00:34:00,010 --> 00:34:00,973
For everything he did,

381
00:34:01,534 --> 00:34:02,930
one death wouldn’t be enough
to pay for it.

382
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:07,440
We all know he is responsible
for all his crimes.

383
00:34:08,400 --> 00:34:10,798
Are we really working our butts off
to save the worst guy ever?

384
00:34:17,154 --> 00:34:17,899
Listen.

385
00:34:19,042 --> 00:34:21,697
I want you all to go back to
the most basic question:

386
00:34:23,029 --> 00:34:25,401
What is a police officer’s duty?

387
00:34:37,690 --> 00:34:38,400
Excuse me.

388
00:34:38,540 --> 00:34:41,600
Can you show me the crime scenes
of all three cases again?

389
00:34:49,750 --> 00:34:50,699
An abandoned warehouse,

390
00:34:51,102 --> 00:34:51,900
a field,

391
00:34:52,660 --> 00:34:54,000
and a warehouse by the river.

392
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:56,240
Those are the three locations
the murderer chose.

393
00:34:57,711 --> 00:34:59,401
Memorials of Evil.

394
00:35:01,031 --> 00:35:01,798
What’s that?

395
00:35:02,811 --> 00:35:03,601
Oh, right.

396
00:35:03,697 --> 00:35:06,880
The notebook at Kim’s place
jogged my memory.

397
00:35:07,380 --> 00:35:11,189
Memorials of Evil is a name used to mark
the locations where the bodies are found

398
00:35:11,216 --> 00:35:12,900
in the Nekros manga.

399
00:35:13,414 --> 00:35:19,096
These places are well thought out
and make sense for each victim.

400
00:35:26,084 --> 00:35:28,574
Uh, yes, I did come up with it,

401
00:35:28,630 --> 00:35:32,229
but I think the murderer
used the same logic

402
00:35:32,250 --> 00:35:33,204
to deal with the bodies.

403
00:35:33,644 --> 00:35:36,598
Do you have all three victims’ profiles?

404
00:35:37,807 --> 00:35:38,574
Of course.

405
00:35:50,297 --> 00:35:51,640
What do you think, Inspector?

406
00:36:05,976 --> 00:36:07,302
We’re on the same page, aren’t we?

407
00:36:07,496 --> 00:36:08,902
I believe we are.

408
00:36:10,950 --> 00:36:15,800
Can you please explain how you understand
the idea of Memorials of Evil?

409
00:36:16,710 --> 00:36:17,902
From my understanding,

410
00:36:19,390 --> 00:36:22,819
each crime scene has
something to do with the cases

411
00:36:22,844 --> 00:36:24,600
the victims were involved in.

412
00:36:24,859 --> 00:36:26,798
And according to the manga Nekros,

413
00:36:27,915 --> 00:36:29,897
those places would be called
Memorials of Evil

414
00:36:31,401 --> 00:36:32,502
In other words,

415
00:36:33,069 --> 00:36:35,560
these are the places the victims
once used for their own gain.

416
00:36:36,524 --> 00:36:37,497
Am I correct?

417
00:36:38,557 --> 00:36:39,302
Exactly.

418
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:41,690
For example, the first case
is the businessman.

419
00:36:41,870 --> 00:36:43,297
The body was found
at an abandoned warehouse.

420
00:36:43,562 --> 00:36:48,240
He was the businessman behind
a swindling case with over 40,000 victims,

421
00:36:48,570 --> 00:36:50,382
where he refused to pay
for his employees’ compensation.

422
00:36:50,420 --> 00:36:52,475
And that factory…

423
00:36:52,499 --> 00:36:54,500
is now the abandoned warehouse
which is the crime scene.

424
00:36:54,515 --> 00:36:55,402
Am I right?

425
00:36:56,352 --> 00:36:59,200
The second victim was
a former Permanent Secretary.

426
00:36:59,514 --> 00:37:01,800
And his body was found in a field.

427
00:37:01,980 --> 00:37:04,102
Oh, I remember this case
because I was investigating it.

428
00:37:04,580 --> 00:37:07,697
The field where the body was found
was expropriated

429
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:09,497
when the victim was in office.

430
00:37:09,810 --> 00:37:10,840
It was huge on the news.

431
00:37:11,260 --> 00:37:12,703
There was a scramble on the land,

432
00:37:12,911 --> 00:37:15,410
and next thing we knew,
the land was passed on to some investors.

433
00:37:15,640 --> 00:37:16,675
What about the third case?

434
00:37:17,712 --> 00:37:18,640
Attorney Komkrit.

435
00:37:18,866 --> 00:37:20,004
What do you think, Inspector?

436
00:37:20,410 --> 00:37:21,699
What’s the connection here?

437
00:37:24,435 --> 00:37:25,800
This warehouse by the pier

438
00:37:26,137 --> 00:37:29,398
was once where the biggest stash of drugs
in our country’s history was hidden.

439
00:37:29,950 --> 00:37:31,802
It belonged to one of Komkrit’s clients.

440
00:37:32,434 --> 00:37:34,080
Of course the charges were dropped.

441
00:37:35,903 --> 00:37:37,102
The fourth case…

442
00:37:38,660 --> 00:37:39,730
MP Jaratphong.

443
00:37:44,594 --> 00:37:49,896
I think MP Jaratphong is like
a corpse amped up on formalin

444
00:37:50,131 --> 00:37:51,700
and dressed up to look presentable.

445
00:37:52,465 --> 00:37:55,099
From the outside,
he’s shining and glorious,

446
00:37:55,761 --> 00:37:56,897
but inside, he’s rotten.

447
00:37:59,034 --> 00:38:00,099
That’s why I think

448
00:38:00,709 --> 00:38:05,002
the crime scene Nekros means
for MP Jaratphong must be…

449
00:38:08,007 --> 00:38:09,360
The temple he built.

450
00:38:24,620 --> 00:38:25,345
Inspector.

451
00:38:25,670 --> 00:38:27,001
Thank you for believing me.

452
00:38:28,294 --> 00:38:29,902
I told you I believe you.

453
00:38:31,860 --> 00:38:32,840
Why?

454
00:38:34,280 --> 00:38:35,198
No reason.

455
00:39:29,410 --> 00:39:31,998
I knew we’d find a body.

456
00:39:35,497 --> 00:39:36,500
Secure all exits.

457
00:39:36,591 --> 00:39:37,802
The murderer is still inside the temple.

458
00:39:41,705 --> 00:39:42,401
Damn it.

459
00:39:42,992 --> 00:39:44,197
It’s the same damn trick.

460
00:39:44,850 --> 00:39:46,042
What a scum.

461
00:40:12,176 --> 00:40:12,900
Hey!

462
00:40:19,957 --> 00:40:20,900
Hey! Stop!

463
00:40:29,597 --> 00:40:30,398
Kaye!

464
00:40:59,762 --> 00:41:00,601
Let go of me!

465
00:41:02,125 --> 00:41:02,983
Let go!

466
00:41:13,382 --> 00:41:14,053
Phat?

467
00:41:14,075 --> 00:41:15,402
Phat. Phat. Phat.

468
00:41:15,503 --> 00:41:16,100
Phat!

469
00:41:16,358 --> 00:41:17,102
Phat!

470
00:41:17,946 --> 00:41:18,804
Ph…

471
00:41:19,620 --> 00:41:20,182
Phat!
Phat!

472
00:41:21,259 --> 00:41:22,001
Shit!

473
00:41:22,524 --> 00:41:23,840
Phat. Phat. Phat.

474
00:41:24,561 --> 00:41:25,299
Phat.

475
00:41:30,099 --> 00:41:31,200
Phat. Phat.

476
00:41:31,672 --> 00:41:32,380
Phat.

477
00:41:32,912 --> 00:41:34,099
Phat. Phat. Phat.

478
00:41:35,297 --> 00:41:36,303
Phat. Phat.

479
00:41:37,272 --> 00:41:38,000
Phat!

480
00:41:39,137 --> 00:41:39,900
Phat!

481
00:41:40,054 --> 00:41:40,903
Shit!

482
00:41:41,491 --> 00:41:42,300
Phat!

483
00:41:44,930 --> 00:41:45,700
Shit…

484
00:41:47,860 --> 00:41:48,703
Phat. Phat.

485
00:41:49,856 --> 00:41:50,601
Phat!

486
00:42:10,546 --> 00:42:11,500
Show me your wound.

487
00:42:23,697 --> 00:42:25,299
Why did you run after him?

488
00:42:26,540 --> 00:42:27,800
What if he has a gun?

489
00:42:28,570 --> 00:42:30,100
What if he shoots at you?

490
00:42:30,825 --> 00:42:31,804
What will you do?

491
00:42:32,066 --> 00:42:32,802
Well…

492
00:42:33,670 --> 00:42:35,398
I saw he was running.

493
00:42:36,830 --> 00:42:38,576
When it comes to hunting
the murderer down,

494
00:42:38,657 --> 00:42:40,040
let me handle it.

495
00:42:41,100 --> 00:42:42,402
Your job

496
00:42:43,668 --> 00:42:46,998
is to stay alive until all this is over.

497
00:42:48,002 --> 00:42:48,899
Got it?

498
00:42:58,970 --> 00:43:00,096
See you at the car.

499
00:43:00,751 --> 00:43:01,899
I’ll give you a ride home.

500
00:43:18,270 --> 00:43:19,397
Thank you

501
00:43:20,259 --> 00:43:22,200
for risking your life to save me.

502
00:43:22,620 --> 00:43:23,400
Worried about me?

503
00:43:24,725 --> 00:43:26,450
You’re thinking
his life’s miserable, aren’t you?

504
00:43:26,748 --> 00:43:29,602
Do you really believe Kim is Nekros?

505
00:43:29,783 --> 00:43:32,598
Cops can’t decide based on feelings.

506
00:43:32,822 --> 00:43:35,299
Do you think Mr. Kill is proud of me?

507
00:43:35,447 --> 00:43:37,302
If Kim wasn’t in custody right now,

508
00:43:37,374 --> 00:43:39,002
who would be the next victim?

509
00:43:39,680 --> 00:43:42,800
There are still so many things
Kaye doesn't know about.

510
00:43:43,182 --> 00:43:46,280
For example… Your father’s case.
